<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jorge Luis Borges</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1986">1986</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jorge Luis Borges was an Argentine writer whose short-story collections Ficciones (1944) and The Aleph (1949), with their labyrinths, mirrors and imaginary books, made him one of the most influential authors of the twentieth century. He was also a poet and essayist, and served as director of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>'s National Library from 1955 to 1973.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jorge-luis-borges.jpg" alt="Jorge Luis Borges" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Grete Stern · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jorge_Luis_Borges_1951,_by_Grete_Stern_(full).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
